window.EN={"1":"Prince Celice's Liberation Army and its exploits encouraged the people suffering under the Empire's tyranny,","2":"and uprisings among the people broke out one after another across the land.","3":"But most of them, lacking any unity, were easily crushed,","4":"and great numbers of people fell victim to the Empire's soldiers.","5":"On the Thracia Peninsula, in the kingdom of Leonster,","6":"Quan's son, Prince Leaf, had raised an army with Finn's help,","7":"but suffered a crushing defeat before King Bloom's great host, and was now isolated deep in enemy territory.","8":"At the temple ruling the Yied Desert was Kutuzov of the Loptr cult,","9":"and in the oasis town of Darna","10":"were the merchant-turned-lord Bramsel and the mercenary captain Jabarro,","11":"while at Melgen Castle were Prince Ishtore and the capable lady general Raiza,","12":"and in the capital Alster were Bloom, son of Duke Reptor,","13":"and his niece, the mage girl Tinny.","14":"Meanwhile, in the city of Ribot, the warriors of the Isaac Liberation Army, led by Celice,","15":"were preparing to set out to save their distant comrades in Leonster.","16":"Each carrying their own private hopes in their hearts,","17":"Celice and his companions' new battle was now about to begin.","18":"(Leaf): Finn, how do things stand? Is there still no word from the unit we sent ahead?","19":"(Finn): ...Unfortunately, the uprising has failed. The unit that went to attack Alster was wiped out entirely.","20":"(Finn): We no longer have a single soldier left.","21":"(Leaf): No... just when our chance had finally come, was it all for nothing...","22":"(Leaf): Damn it, Bloom... next time, I'll be the one who faces you!","23":"(Finn): Prince Leaf, please calm yourself. This isn't over yet. Remember the promise we made with Lord Levin —","24":"(Finn): that Lord Celice's Liberation Army is heading for Leonster, and that until then, we must hold on no matter what.","25":"(Leaf): Prince Celice... the orphaned child of Lord Sigurd, my father's close friend, and Princess Deirdre, they say...","26":"(Leaf): I'd like to meet him... if we join our strength together, we might be able to save the people suffering under the Empire's tyranny.","27":"(Nanna): That's right, Lord Leaf. If we lose you here too, the soldiers' deaths will have been for nothing.","28":"(Nanna): For now, let's abandon this castle and go into hiding somewhere around the church to the west.","29":"(Leaf): I suppose... that might be one option.","30":"(Leaf): Alright, in any case, let's hold out a little longer... at least until I can meet Prince Celice...","31":"(Bloom): What is going on? Why can't you take even such a small castle? Are you lot even trying!","32":"(Philip): Haa... but, breaking through the enemy's defensive line has proven extremely difficult...","33":"(Bloom): Fools! I don't want to hear excuses — hurry up and take Leonster Castle!","34":"(Bloom): If we dawdle, the Isaac rebels will come!","35":"(Philip): Yes sir, we'll set out at once.","36":"(Patty): Just as the rumors said, there was a ton of treasure here — it's been a good while since I've had such a good haul.","37":"(Patty): Well, no time to stand around admiring it — better make a quick getaway.","38":"(Shanan): Hey, wait. Everything else can go, but that sword — hand it over to me.","39":"(Patty): What's with you? You trying to swipe my hard-earned loot?","40":"(Patty): No way, this sword was the one I worked hardest for — if you want it, come and get it, you dummy.","41":"(Shanan): W-, wait!","42":"(Kutuzov): What? The treasury's been ransacked by thieves, you say?","43":"(Kutuzov): Even the Balmung was stolen!? You fools, chase after them at once!","44":"(Dark Priest): Hah, but Lord Kutuzov,","45":"(Dark Priest): with your dark sorcery, surely mere thieves would be dealt with in a single blow, wouldn't they?","46":"(Kutuzov): The magic of Fenrir, you mean... I know that well enough, but I can't find the tome. I've ordered my men to search for it, but...","47":"(Dark Priest): Understood. Then let us and the mercenaries go after them.","48":"(Dark Priest): There's no need to worry. We'll retrieve the stolen treasure in no time.","49":"(Celice): To reach Leonster, we have to cross this vast desert, don't we...","50":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right... and on top of that, the Temple of Yied is now under the Loptr cult's control,","51":"(Levin (Strategist)): and they say dark sorcerers there show no mercy to anyone who tries to cross the desert.","52":"(Levin (Strategist)): These days the Yied Desert is known as the Desert of Death.","53":"(Celice): Then travelers must be in real trouble. Isn't there some way we could take the Temple of Yied?","54":"(Levin (Strategist)): Heh... I thought you'd say that. There is a way, but it won't be easy — we'll have to be prepared for considerable losses.","55":"(Celice): I understand that. But I can't just leave it be.","56":"(Celice): Shanan's safety weighs on my mind too — first, let's aim to take Yied. Everything starts from there!","57":"(Soldier): Lord Bramsel, it seems the Isaac rebels have made their move.","58":"(Bramsel): The rebels, you say? That brat they call Celice? Hehehe... now this is interesting.","59":"(Bramsel): There's a hefty bounty on that fellow's head — I'd love to be the one to finish him off myself.","60":"(Bramsel): Alright, I have a good plan. For now, let's seal the border and watch how things go — the moment they tire themselves out from fighting will be our chance.","61":"(Bramsel): Tell Jabarro's mercenaries not to slack off on their preparations!","62":"(Lene): Hmm, things have gotten noisy around here lately. Could it be that a war's started or something?","63":"(Ares): It's nothing that grand. We're just preparing in case the Isaac rebels show up.","64":"(Lene): Oh, I see, that's good. I was a little worried whether you'd be going too, Ares.","65":"(Ares): If it comes to a fight, I'll go — I am a mercenary, after all. And besides, I hear the one leading the rebels is that Sigurd's son...","66":"(Ares): If I can, I'd like to be the one to strike him down with my own hand. He's my father's enemy, after all...","67":"(Lene): Ahaha, you're still saying things like that. Silly man,","68":"(Lene): your father, and that Sigurd fellow too, were both knights, weren't they.","69":"(Lene): In that case, isn't killing people just their job?","70":"(Lene): Even I don't like dancing in front of those sleazy men, but I put up with it because it's my job too.","71":"(Lene): There's no helping it if you want to go on living — holding a grudge over that isn't very manly, if you ask me.","72":"(Ares): Lene... alright, I understand. I'll think about it a little more. I... I know, really...","73":"(Dark Priest): Lord Kutuzov, we've found the Fenrir tome.","74":"(Kutuzov): What? You finally found it! Hehehe... this is the end for them now.","75":"(Kutuzov): Let them learn well just how terrifying Fenrir truly is.","76":"(Patty): Eek, stop it! I won't be able to get married!","77":"(Shanan): Don't be absurd, I'm not going to do anything to you. I just want that sword back.","78":"(Patty): Give it back... wait, this is yours?","79":"(Shanan): That's right, it's the holy sword Balmung, passed down in my family for generations.","80":"(Shanan): No one but me can use it — it's worthless in your hands.","81":"(Patty): But then, how did this sword-whatchamacallit end up in Yied?","82":"(Shanan): When Grannvale invaded Isaac, my father fell in battle, and the sword was carried off somewhere.","83":"(Shanan): I only recently heard that it was here in Yied. So I came to take it back.","84":"(Patty): Wait, could it be... you're that Prince Shanan of Isaac?","85":"(Shanan): That's right...","86":"(Patty): Ehh, really!? Whoa, lucky me!","87":"(Shanan): .........","88":"(Patty): You know, I've always admired Prince Shanan — I thought, just once, I'd love to meet him... or something like that.","89":"(Shanan): .........","90":"(Patty): But to actually get to meet you for real, how wonderful is that.","91":"(Shanan): ...Alright, I understand that already. So, my sword, please.","92":"(Patty): Oh, sorry, here, this is it, right.","93":"(Shanan): Balmung... finally back in my hands... this is... the holy sword's... ah, what power...","94":"(Patty): Ahh, swoon...","95":"(Oifey): Delmud, I heard your sister is in Leonster?","96":"(Delmud): Yes, we were separated when we were small, but recently I learned she's with Finn, the Leonster knight.","97":"(Oifey): I see, so it's with Lord Finn... you must want to see her, then.","98":"(Delmud): Yes, as soon as possible!","99":"(Oifey): Mm, then you'll need to work hard too. Let me teach you a bit of swordsmanship.","100":"(Delmud): Yes! Please do!!","101":"(Celice): Shanan! Thank goodness, you're safe!","102":"(Shanan): Yeah, sorry to have worried you.","103":"(Shanan): I hear that while I was away, you took back Isaac. My thanks, Celice.","104":"(Celice): No, that was all thanks to your strength too, Shanan. Because you were there, everyone was able to do their best.","105":"(Shanan): You've grown strong, Celice. I see... so this is finally...","106":"(Celice): Shanan...?","107":"(Shanan): Hm? ...no, it's nothing. Don't worry about it.","108":"(Celice): Shanan, I'm going to fight the Empire! Is that alright with you?","109":"(Shanan): Heh, of course, Celice. I've been waiting for this day too.","110":"(Celice): Shanan, thank you!","111":"(Lakche): Prince Shanan!! Thank goodness... you're safe!","112":"(Shanan): Lakche — it seems things were quite difficult here. Sorry for leaving you all behind.","113":"(Lakche): No, as long as you're safe, Lord Shanan, I...","114":"(Shanan): Has your swordsmanship improved a little?","115":"(Lakche): I still can't hold a candle to you, my prince.","116":"(Shanan): Then let me teach you a bit. It looks like you're lacking strength — put more spirit into your swing.","117":"(Lakche): Ah, yes! Like this...?","118":"(Soldier): By Lord Bramsel's orders, we can't let you pass through here — best you leave at once.","119":"(Kutuzov): You rebels... defiling the sacred Temple of Yied!","120":"(Kutuzov): Damn you, I'll have you buried in dark magic!","121":"(Kutuzov): To the Loptr Empire... glory be...","122":"(Celice): So this is the Temple of Yied... what terrible ruin...","123":"(Levin (Strategist)): For a long time, the remnants of the Loptr Empire hid away in the depths beneath this temple.","124":"(Levin (Strategist)): Because if they went up to the surface, they'd be persecuted and burned at the stake.","125":"(Levin (Strategist)): They probably weren't evil from the very start either, but the long years turned them into devils.","126":"(Celice): ...even if their ancestors cooperated with the Empire, it's too cruel to lay that sin on their descendants, all these years later.","127":"(Celice): And on top of that, to be called a dark cult, or the kin of an evil god — it must have been painful for them.","128":"(Celice): This graffiti on the wall looks like a child drew it, but it's praying for the dark god's resurrection.","129":"(Celice): To them, is Loptous really their one and only god...","130":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right, Celice. Good and evil aren't something that can be weighed so simply.","131":"(Levin (Strategist)): What we should hate is the wicked heart, not the people themselves. Don't ever forget that...","132":"(Bramsel): So Yied has fallen, has it... hehehe... this works out well for us. Alright, open the border.","133":"(Bramsel): Let them push on ahead. Either way, there's no chance they can take Melgen — once they're worn out, we'll strike them from behind.","134":"(Bramsel): Kukuku, nothing could be simpler. Isn't that right, Jabarro?","135":"(Jabarro): Heh, as unchanged as ever, aren't you, Lord Bramsel...","136":"(Jabarro): Well, we're mercenaries too — as long as we're paid, we have no complaints. We'll put on a fine show for you.","137":"(Ishtore): What, the rebels have taken Yied, you say? Hmm, Raiza, what do you think?","138":"(Raiza): I believe they'll head to relieve Leonster.","139":"(Raiza): Your father seems fully occupied with the conquest of Leonster,","140":"(Raiza): and letting an enemy in behind Alster would be dangerous.","141":"(Raiza): I think we should meet them here at Melgen with our full strength.","142":"(Ishtore): I see... I must go help my father, Raiza — can you take command of the troops and hold our defenses firm?","143":"(Raiza): Yes, leave it to me!","144":"(Ishtore): I don't want to put you in danger, but there's no one else I can trust with this. I'm sorry, Raiza.","145":"(Raiza): You flatter me... but please, don't worry about someone like me.","146":"(Raiza): Lord Ishtore, please take care above all. Now then... Raiza's unit, moving out!","147":"(Bramsel): Ho ho ho, Lene, that was quite a fine dance. Come here, I'll give you a reward.","148":"(Lene): How rude. If you want something, come here yourself!","149":"(Bramsel): Hoho, that fiery spirit is rather charming too. But you'd better learn how to talk properly — hey, drag that little girl over here!","150":"(Lene): Wh-, what are you doing! Let go of me! You idiot!!","151":"(Ares): Stop it! You bastards!! Take your hands off her.","152":"(Bramsel): What? Who are you!? A mere mercenary, daring to defy me!?","153":"(Ares): I won't allow anyone to lay a hand on Lene!","154":"(Bramsel): Wh-, what did you say, damn it, damn it... hey, someone, finish him off!","155":"(Ares): Can't you see this sword? The cursed blade Mystletainn thirsts for human blood.","156":"(Ares): Do you really want to become its prey so needlessly?","157":"(Bramsel): Th-, the cursed blade Mystletainn, you say!? ...y-, you... could it be...","158":"(Ares): That's right. I am the Black Knight Ares.","159":"(Bramsel): I, I understand... sorry... it was just a little joke, I swear — I'll never lay a hand on this girl again, so please forgive me.","160":"(Ares): Good, as long as you understand. Lene, are you alright?","161":"(Lene): Yeah... Ares, thank you...","162":"(Bramsel): Damn, damn it, making a fool of me... just you wait...","163":"— (only shown if neither Patty nor Celice has a sweetheart)","164":"(Patty): Eek, it's Lord Celice!","165":"(Celice): Huh? And you are...?","166":"(Patty): I'm Patty, Lord Shanan's sweetheart.","167":"(Celice): Shanan's... that's a lie, isn't it.","168":"(Patty): Ahaha, caught me, huh? I used to be a thief, but I've decided to go straight now.","169":"(Patty): So I'll help out the Liberation Army.","170":"(Celice): Eh, you will? But this is an army — it's dangerous here, you know.","171":"(Patty): Oh, is that really something you should be saying? You lot don't have any money, do you — you can't fight a war without it.","172":"(Patty): If I'm around, I can earn you as much as you need.","173":"(Celice): But stealing is wrong.","174":"(Patty): You don't know anything, do you, Lord Celice. All that gold the imperial soldiers carry — they stole it from the people by force.","175":"(Patty): So why is it wrong to try and take it back!","176":"(Patty): I just want to give it back to everyone, that's all...","177":"(Celice): I see, I didn't realize... sorry, Patty.","178":"(Patty): No... sniff, sniff...","179":"(Celice): Patty, I'd like you to lend us your strength.","180":"(Patty): Eh, really? ...you mean it!?","181":"(Celice): Of course.","182":"(Patty): Lord Celice! I'll do my best, okay.","183":"(Patty): Oh, that's right! As a token of our new friendship, take this sword.","184":"(Celice): This is... quite a sword.","185":"(Patty): It's called the Hero's Sword. For Lord Celice, I give it to you, with a kiss ♥","186":"(Raiza): Rebels, is it... I'm sorry, but your advance ends here.","187":"(Raiza): As long as I, Raiza, am here, I won't let you through to Melgen Castle.","188":"(Raiza): Ahh, Lord Ishtore...","189":"— (only if Raiza is still alive)","190":"(Ishtore): Heh, impressive that you've made it this far. I'll give you that much credit.","191":"— (only if Raiza has died)","192":"(Ishtore): You rebels... how dare you... Raiza... I'll never forgive you!","193":"(Ishtore): Raiza... I...","194":"(Levin (Strategist)): We've finally made it to Melgen. Celice, Leonster is close now.","195":"(Celice): Levin, how much longer will fighting like this go on...","196":"(Celice): That lady general, and Prince Ishtore too — I don't think either of them were really bad people...","197":"(Levin (Strategist)): But they were helping King Bloom, who tormented the people.","198":"(Levin (Strategist)): There's no mistaking that they were our enemy.","199":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, we're not fighting out of hatred alone — this is a war.","200":"(Celice): I know, but...","201":"(Levin (Strategist)): Hahaha, well, it's fine. That's one of your good qualities. But don't let it weigh on you forever.","202":"(Levin (Strategist)): Right now we have a great purpose — rescuing Leonster — to focus on.","203":"(Celice): You're right, I understand, Levin. Let's go to Leonster. Everything starts from there.","204":"(Bramsel): What did you say, Melgen has fallen? Damn it, so we were too late after all! But they can't have fully recovered yet either.","205":"(Bramsel): Alright, now's our chance. Jabarro's unit, move out!","206":"(Bramsel): Strike them from behind while their guard is down, and kill every last one of them!","207":"(Jabarro): Understood!","208":"(Lene): Are you really going, no matter what? Even after all my pleading...","209":"(Ares): I owe Jabarro a debt. He took me in and raised me...","210":"(Lene): That man's just using you. I... I hate him.","211":"(Ares): ...Lene... but still...","212":"(Lene): Fine, whatever... if you like him that much, do as you please.","213":"(Lene): I don't care anymore!","214":"(Ares): Lene...","215":"(Bramsel): Kukuku... so Ares went off, did he... what a fool...","216":"(Bloom): Vampa, Fetra, Elu! Move out.","217":"(Bloom): Show them just how terrifying you three truly are.","218":"(Fetra): Yes sir, leave it to us, Lord Bloom!","219":"(Vampa): We won't disappoint you.","220":"(Elu): We have no intention of living through this shamefully without crushing the rebels!","221":"(Bloom): Good, I'm counting on you. Tinny, you'll go too, won't you.","222":"(Tinny): ...if that's what you wish, uncle...","223":"(Bloom): Mm, you lost your mother and became an orphan, and I was the one who took you in and raised you.","224":"(Bloom): I trust you haven't forgotten that debt.","225":"(Tinny): Yes...","226":"(Bloom): Good, then go. They even killed my son Ishtore — along with his sweetheart Raiza.","227":"(Bloom): You're the one to avenge that grudge.","228":"(Bloom): Alright, all of you go too — wipe out every last one of the enemy!","229":"(Fetra): Fetra, Elu, you understand, don't you — don't forget, the three of us work together.","230":"(Fetra): It's us who'll be the ones to take Celice's head! I won't lose to Tinny's unit.","231":"(Tinny): The townspeople call them the Liberation Army... but my brother Ishtore was killed by them.","232":"(Tinny): I don't understand... what should I do... tell me, mother...","233":"(Bramsel): Little girl, the other day you shamed me thoroughly — I'll make sure to pay you back in full.","234":"(Lene): What, what do you intend to do to me.","235":"(Lene): Now that Ares is gone, you've suddenly grown bold — as cowardly as ever.","236":"(Lene): But I won't let you have your way with me!","237":"(Bramsel): Damn you! Well, no matter — I'll make you regret it thoroughly later. For now, throw her in the dungeon!","238":"(Lene): Ahh......Ares...","239":"(Jabarro): Ares, for a man like you to lose your head over a woman like that — what's gotten into you.","240":"(Jabarro): Well, never mind. It's over and done with now, so let's forget about it.","241":"(Ares): Over and done with? Jabarro, what do you mean by that?","242":"(Jabarro): Hehehe... that woman, right about now, is probably with Bramsel...","243":"(Ares): Wh-, surely not... Jabarro! You knew about this and kept quiet!","244":"(Jabarro): Leave women to be played with, that's all — they're not suited for you.","245":"(Ares): You bastard! ...I've misjudged you... I'm going back to Darna! ...I'm taking Lene back!","246":"(Jabarro): That won't do. Whoever defies my orders, I show no mercy — whoever they are.","247":"(Jabarro): Ares, even if that's you.","248":"(Ares): ...I owe you a great deal. But this is where it ends.","249":"(Ares): I'm going. Anyone who tries to stop me will have to face Mystletainn!","250":"(Jabarro): Heh, you brat! Don't get carried away with yourself!!","251":"(Ares): So you're Celice...","252":"(Celice): And you are...?","253":"(Ares): The Black Knight Ares... but you'd understand better if I said I'm Eltshan's son.","254":"(Celice): Eh!? ...don't tell me, King Noddion... Eltshan's...!?","255":"(Ares): That's right! Eltshan, who was killed by your father, was my father!","256":"(Ares): My mother died still holding a grudge against Sigurd... do you understand that bitterness!","257":"(Celice): I see... but Ares, your father and my father Sigurd were close friends.","258":"(Celice): It ended in tragedy, but I'm sure they never held any grudge against each other.","259":"(Ares): Nonsense... Sigurd is my father's enemy — that's what I've believed my whole life, living by it!","260":"(Celice): Ares, give me just a little time — stay with this army for a while. I think your misunderstanding will clear up.","261":"(Celice): Just like my father, I respect King Eltshan too. Ares, please, I beg you, try to understand.","262":"(Ares): Celice... alright... I'll wait and see for a while.","263":"(Ares): But if I find out what you've said is a lie, then be ready — I'll take your life in Sigurd's place.","264":"(Ares): Got it, Celice!","265":"(Celice): If that time comes, do as you wish.","266":"(Celice): Ares... I think meeting you is something my father and the others would be happiest about, more than anything. Somehow, I can't help but feel that way...","267":"(Leaf): Lord Celice, it's an honor to meet you. I am the son of Quan, King of Leonster.","268":"(Celice): Prince Leaf, I'm glad we could meet. Thank goodness you're safe.","269":"(Leaf): In the battle of Belhalla, my parents fell by Thracia's treachery,","270":"(Leaf): and my homeland Leonster was occupied by Duke Bloom's imperial army.","271":"(Leaf): I was saved by the knight Finn, and while hidden away in a village in the countryside, I kept waiting for the day my homeland would be liberated.","272":"(Leaf): And at last, that chance came...","273":"(Celice): ...I heard that many people who rose up with you, Prince, were killed by King Bloom.","274":"(Celice): When I think that if we had come just a little sooner, I can't help but regret it deeply.","275":"(Leaf): No, Lord Celice, it was my own strength that was lacking.","276":"(Leaf): But I too am the son of Quan, known as the Knight of Nordion.","277":"(Leaf): I want to live in a way that won't shame my father.","278":"(Leaf): Please, let me join your Liberation Army.","279":"(Leaf): To bring the light back to Grannvale, I too, for whatever little I can do, wish to be of help.","280":"(Celice): Thank you, Prince Leaf.","281":"(Celice): I've heard that our fathers were close friends who shared life and death together.","282":"(Celice): And your mother is my aunt.","283":"(Celice): But both of them lost their lives trying to save my father...","284":"(Celice): Prince Leaf, I am truly sorry. Let me apologize on my father's behalf...","285":"(Leaf): Lord Celice, I am proud of my parents, and I respect Lord Sigurd too.","286":"(Leaf): The ones I hate are Emperor Arvis, and that King Travant!!","287":"(Celice): I feel the very same way...","288":"(Celice): Prince Leaf, I want to carry on our fathers' will and bring light back to this world. Please, lend me your strength.","289":"(Leaf): Yes! Lord Celice!!","290":"— (only if Nanna's father is Finn)","291":"(Finn): Nanna, are you alright?","292":"(Nanna): Yes, father — there's no need to worry about me.","293":"(Finn): You're as strong-willed as ever. You're starting to resemble Lachesis more and more.","294":"(Nanna): Father, you loved mother deeply, didn't you — then why did you let her go off alone!","295":"(Finn): That business of Lachesis going to Isaac... don't bring that up again.","296":"(Finn): Even if you're my child, I'd rather you didn't pry into matters between husband and wife.","297":"(Nanna): But...","298":"(Finn): Someday you'll understand too — once you've grown up...","299":"— (only if Lakche's father is Finn)","300":"(Finn): ! ...you are...!?","301":"(Lakche): Eh? I'm Lakche, but...","302":"(Finn): C-, could it be...","303":"(Lakche): Is something wrong? Being stared at like that is a bit troubling.","304":"(Finn): No... sorry... you just resemble someone I knew, so closely...","305":"(Lakche): Eh? Me...?","306":"(Finn): Mm... it's an embarrassing thing to say, but you look just like someone I loved long ago.","307":"(Lakche): Was she your sweetheart?","308":"(Finn): Yes, but we were separated by the war. I've been searching for her ever since...","309":"(Lakche): I see, that's a sad story... so, what was her name...?","310":"(Finn): Ayra... she was a beautiful woman, who looked just like you...","311":"(Lakche): What, Ayra, you said!? ...c-, could it be...","312":"— (only if Nanna's father is Finn)","313":"(Finn): ! ...you are...!?","314":"(Nanna): Eh, I'm Nanna, but... you must be Lord Finn.","315":"(Finn): You...","316":"(Nanna): Is something wrong? Being stared at like that is a bit troubling.","317":"(Finn): No... sorry... you just resemble someone I knew, so closely...","318":"(Nanna): Eh? Me...","319":"(Finn): ...it's an embarrassing thing to say, but you look just like someone I loved long ago.","320":"(Nanna): Was she your sweetheart?","321":"(Finn): Yes... but we were separated by the war. I've been searching for her ever since...","322":"(Nanna): I see... how sad for you... so, what was her name...?","323":"(Finn): Ethlyn... she was a beautiful woman, who looked just like you...","324":"(Nanna): Ethlyn!? ...mother...!?","325":"(Nanna): (Since Ethlyn's survival is confirmed, I would have liked to see Finn's reunion scene.)","326":"(Rodolvan): Hey, Tristan, listen to me for a second.","327":"(Tristan): What is it, Rodolvan? Need something?","328":"(Rodolvan): Don't say \"what is it\" like that!","329":"(Rodolvan): Well, never mind — by the way, don't you think we're kind of holding Lord Celice back?","330":"(Tristan): We? Wait, am I included in that too? Don't joke around — I'm doing a fine job.","331":"(Rodolvan): Oh really, then what exactly have you done so far? Go on, tell me!","332":"(Tristan): Eh, well, that's... um...","333":"(Rodolvan): See, if you have to think hard to remember, that's proof you haven't done anything worth mentioning, isn't it?","334":"(Tristan): Fine, I admit it! ...so, what do you want me to do about it?","335":"(Rodolvan): How about the two of us do some sword training together? Honestly I don't really want to, with someone like you,","336":"(Rodolvan): but it can't be helped — I want to fight on the front line! Guarding the castle is just not my thing!","337":"(Tristan): You don't even know how to ask someone a favor properly. If you're going to be so reluctant, I won't do it.","338":"(Rodolvan): F-, fine, I get it.","339":"(Rodolvan): Plea~se~ be~ my~ spar~ring~ part~ner. There, happy now!","340":"(Tristan): You've always got one word too many, don't you. Well, fine — once you see how strong I am, you won't be able to talk like that anymore.","341":"(Tristan): Alright then, here I come!","342":"(Rodolvan): Hyah!","343":"(Tristan): Take this!","344":"(Tristan): (If you look closely at the \"two\" in \"the two of us,\" it's actually written in katakana, for some reason.)","345":"(Jabarro): Heh... this is the end for you. Die!","346":"(Jabarro): Damn it... Ares...","347":"(Bramsel): What!? Jabarro, you've botched it.","348":"(Bramsel): Darna is mine — I won't hand it over to anyone!","349":"(Bramsel): Ugh... Darna is mine... mine...","350":"(Celice): So this is the town of Darna...","351":"(Levin (Strategist)): Long ago, during the Holy War, the Liberation Army had a fortress here.","352":"(Levin (Strategist)): Before the Empire's overwhelming military might, the Liberation Army suffered defeat after defeat,","353":"(Levin (Strategist)): and in the end, only a small handful of soldiers held out in the fortress.","354":"(Levin (Strategist)): Wounded, they had resolved themselves to their final battle — but then, a miracle occurred.","355":"(Levin (Strategist)): A god descended from the heavens, and bestowed upon twelve young warriors mysterious weapons and power.","356":"(Levin (Strategist)): In time they came to be called the Twelve Crusaders, and led the Liberation Army into battle.","357":"(Celice): The legendary... miracle of Fort Darna.","358":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's right, and now, once again, a miracle has occurred.","359":"(Levin (Strategist)): With the resurrection of Loptous drawing near, the holy warriors are once more coming back to life...","360":"(Celice): Eh...?","361":"(Levin (Strategist)): Hehehe... well, never mind. You'll understand soon enough...","362":"(Delmud): You're... Nanna?","363":"(Nanna): Yes, that's right, but who are you?","364":"(Delmud): Thank goodness! I finally found you! I'm Delmud, your brother.","365":"(Nanna): Eh? ...it can't be...","366":"(Delmud): I didn't know myself until Lord Levin told me.","367":"(Delmud): In the last war, we children fled to Isaac,","368":"(Delmud): but you, having just been born, went to Leonster together with mother, or so I heard.","369":"(Nanna): You're... my brother... then, what about mother!?","370":"(Delmud): Mother? ...Nanna, what do you mean by that?","371":"(Nanna): When I turned three years old,","372":"(Nanna): mother said she was going to go fetch my brother Delmud, and set off for Isaac.","373":"(Nanna): But she never came back after that. I've been waiting for her ever since...","374":"(Delmud): But mother never arrived here!","375":"(Nanna): That can't be... then, mother is...","376":"(Delmud): Yied is a cursed desert — it would be reckless for anyone to go there alone.","377":"(Nanna): Ahh... mother Lachesis...","378":"(Tristan): You're... Jeanne?","379":"(Jeanne): Yes, that's right, but who are you?","380":"(Tristan): Thank goodness! I finally found you! I'm Tristan, your brother.","381":"(Jeanne): Eh? ...it can't be... you're lying!","382":"(Tristan): It's not a lie. Our father was a knight of the kingdom of Noddion,","383":"(Tristan): but he died in battle during the Agustrian uprising, and we, who were still small, were taken in by Sigurd's army.","384":"(Tristan): After that we fled to Isaac, but you disappeared along the way.","385":"(Jeanne): I see... that explains it. My adoptive father was a traveling merchant, and he told me he'd picked me up in Isaac.","386":"(Tristan): Yeah, I'll bet you got lost, and he must have saved you.","387":"(Jeanne): But that adoptive father of mine was killed by imperial soldiers too. I was saved by Finn when I was seven.","388":"(Tristan): I see, so you had a hard time of it too. I'm sorry, Jeanne...","389":"(Jeanne): No, it's fine. I'm happy, really — because it turns out I had a brother too, after all.","390":"(Jeanne): Please don't go anywhere else ever again, brother Tristan...","391":"(Arthur): Wait... that pendant of yours...","392":"(Tinny): Eh? This is my mother's keepsake, but...","393":"(Arthur): I knew it! You're Tinny, aren't you! Ah, finally, I found you.","394":"(Tinny): Eh, who are you?","395":"(Arthur): Look, this — the same pendant as yours. I've worn it since I was small.","396":"(Tinny): Oh, it really is... but why is that?","397":"(Arthur): My mother was a warrior of the Liberation Army. After the battle, she fled to Silesse, taking me with her,","398":"(Arthur): but she was carried off by someone, along with my newborn little sister, and all that was left to me was this pendant.","399":"(Arthur): Just recently, I learned that it was King Bloom of Alster who took her,","400":"(Arthur): and I heard that mother has already passed away too. But my sister... Tinny, you must still be alive,","401":"(Arthur): and I wanted to see you, so... that's why I came all this way.","402":"(Tinny): That can't be... mother was forced away by uncle Bloom... I didn't know...","403":"(Tinny): But now it makes sense. I don't remember much about mother, but I remember she always seemed sad.","404":"(Tinny): So you're my brother... ahh...","405":"(Arthur): Tinny, please, more than anything, stop fighting and come with us — there's so much I want to talk to you about.","406":"(Tinny): Yes, I don't want to fight either. I'll do as you say, brother.","407":"(Tinny): Um... Lord Celice...","408":"(Celice): Hm? ...and you are?","409":"(Tinny): I'm Tinny... Arthur's little sister...","410":"(Celice): Ah, so you're Tinny. I've heard about you.","411":"(Tinny): Um... I'm so sorry!","412":"(Celice): It's fine, don't worry about it — King Bloom is your uncle, after all, so there was nothing to be done about being on opposite sides.","413":"(Tinny): Will you really forgive me?","414":"(Celice): Of course. You're not a bad person.","415":"(Tinny): Lord Celice, you really are just as I'd heard. I wish I could have met you sooner.","416":"(Celice): Thank you, Tinny. But fighting your own kin must be painful — you don't have to push yourself, you know.","417":"(Tinny): Lord Celice...","418":"(Ares): Lene! Where are you! Where!!","419":"(Lene): Ares...","420":"(Ares): Ah, Lene! Are you alright!","421":"(Lene): I'm not really alright at all... but someone from the Liberation Army saved me. Ares, you came back...","422":"(Ares): I'm sorry... I was... such a fool... I didn't listen to what you said, Lene, and because of that you went through such an awful thing...","423":"(Lene): It's fine... it's over now... Ares, you came back for me, so...","424":"(Ares): I'll never... do that again...","425":"(Lene): ...I won't talk back like a spoiled brat anymore either. So Ares, please don't ever go anywhere again.","426":"(Lene): Nice to meet you, Lord Celice.","427":"(Celice): Ah... y-, you are...","428":"(Lene): I'm Lene, a dancer.","429":"(Celice): So you're... Lene...","430":"(Lene): Oh my, is this the first time you've seen a dancer, Lord Celice?","431":"(Celice): Y-, yeah...","432":"(Lene): Heheh, oh, Lord Celice...","433":"— Who could it be?","434":"(Shanan): Oof!","435":"(Daisy): Hahah! Look at Lord Shanan, so surprised~","436":"(Shanan): D-, Daisy! Phew, I almost ended up killing you there...","437":"(Shanan): Don't joke around like that!","438":"(Daisy): But~, I'm too weak to fight, so I'm bo~red~.","439":"(Shanan): In that case I'll teach you some swordsmanship. There's no time for a proper, full lesson, but you should at least get a bit better.","440":"(Daisy): Yay~! I'm so happy~! A private lesson from Lord Shanan!","441":"(Shanan): I won't teach you if you're not serious about it.","442":"(Daisy): Ye~s♥ I'll be very serious about it~♥","443":"(Shanan): ......alright! First, let's start with your stance — hey, are you even listening!","444":"(Daisy): Swoon ♥","445":"(Fetra): Take this! Elfire!!","446":"(Fetra): Tch, better retreat for now.","447":"(Vampa): Take this! Elwind!!","448":"(Fetra): Tch, better retreat for now.","449":"(Elu): Take this! Elthunder!!","450":"(Fetra): Tch, better retreat for now.","451":"(Bloom): Hehehe... you little brats... with this Thoron Hammer, I have nothing to fear from the likes of you!","452":"(Bloom): Ugh, this can't be happening... it can't be helped... for now, I'll retreat to Conote...","453":"(Celice): Alright, we've taken back Leonster Castle. All that's left is Alster.","454":"(Celice): Everyone, just a little more to endure — let's do our best!","455":"(Levin (Strategist)): Celice, splendidly done. Alster has finally been liberated.","456":"(Celice): But it seems King Bloom has fled to Conote.","457":"(Levin (Strategist)): It can't be helped. The fighting isn't over yet.","458":"(Levin (Strategist)): We've only just gained a foothold on the Thracia Peninsula.","459":"(Celice): Still, the people welcomed us with such enthusiasm — everyone looked so happy...","460":"(Levin (Strategist)): That just shows how terrible the Empire's rule was.","461":"(Levin (Strategist)): The people are putting their hopes in you. The hard part is still ahead of us.","462":"(Celice): Yes... but I have wonderful companions with me.","463":"(Celice): No matter how hard it gets, with them beside me, I believe we can get through it.","464":"(Levin (Strategist)): That's true... with all of you...","465":"(Old woman): Ah, the Liberation Army... Prince Leaf has finally risen up...","466":"(Old woman): Lord Quan... Lady Ethlyn... please, rejoice...","467":"(Old woman): Please, take this Speed Ring, and accept it with my blessing.","468":"(Auntie): We can't endure the Empire's rule any longer. Please, save us...","469":"(Villager (man)): King Bloom is the son of Duke Reptor — after the last war, he conquered this region.","470":"(Villager (man)): But his rule has been terrible... and lately, he's even been trying to take our children away.","471":"(Villager (man)): We just can't put up with it anymore!","472":"(Elder): King Bloom had two children with Queen Hilda — a daughter named Ishtar, and a son named Ishtore,","473":"(Elder): Ishtar is the lord of Manster, while Ishtore, as lord of Melgen, both help their father Bloom,","474":"(Elder): Unlike their father, they're both fine, capable young people. I suppose you'll have to fight them eventually, so be careful.","475":"(Villager (man)): The ones to fear among Bloom's forces are the three sisters, Vampa, Fetra, and Elu, and the mage","476":"(Villager (man)): Tinny. Only, Tinny, despite being Bloom's niece, is a kind-hearted girl.","477":"(Villager (man)): She's helped us out time and again — if only that girl could somehow be spared...","478":"(Villager (woman)): Count Bramsel, the lord of Darna, is just the absolute worst, you know.","479":"(Villager (woman)): He grovels before Grannvale's officials, but acts like he's king in front of us.","480":"(Villager (woman)): I wish someone would hurry up and get rid of that nasty, sleazy man, honestly!","481":"(Elder): Mind you, the mercenary knights Bramsel has hired are tough customers.","482":"(Elder): Among them, there's a man named Ares who's especially fearsome.","483":"(Elder): He's still a young knight, but he carries a cursed blade called Mystletainn.","484":"(Elder): They say he was taken in as a child by the mercenary captain Jabarro, and now he's his most trusted right hand.","485":"(Elder): You won't stand a chance fighting him head-on.","486":"(Elder): That said, I'll give you this Shield Ring — it should be of some use, ho ho ho."};
